    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="concepts" tabindex="-1">Concepts <a class="header-anchor" href="#concepts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Concepts&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This page defines the conceptual vocabulary used across user docs and GATE integration docs.</p><h2 id="the-problem-this-solves" tabindex="-1">The Problem This Solves <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-problem-this-solves" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Problem This Solves&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Without shared definitions, terms like “gating,” “passport,” and “disclosure” become overloaded and documentation becomes inconsistent.</p><h2 id="why-this-matters" tabindex="-1">Why This Matters <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-this-matters" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why This Matters&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Precise terminology improves execution safety, integration correctness, and support quality.</p><h2 id="proof-aware-execution" tabindex="-1">Proof-Aware Execution <a class="header-anchor" href="#proof-aware-execution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Proof-Aware Execution&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Proof-aware execution means the system can require or evaluate verification artifacts depending on the specific flow.</p><h3 id="problem-it-solves" tabindex="-1">Problem it solves <a class="header-anchor" href="#problem-it-solves" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Problem it solves&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Avoids a false binary where all routes are treated as either fully strict-gated or entirely unguided.</p><h3 id="why-it-matters" tabindex="-1">Why it matters <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-it-matters" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why it matters&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Real products need multiple modes:</p><ul><li>strict gating for high-assurance actions</li><li>advisory checks for risk signaling</li><li>wallet-first flows with post-action reconciliation</li></ul><h2 id="session-keys" tabindex="-1">Session Keys <a class="header-anchor" href="#session-keys" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Session Keys&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Session keys are bounded delegation credentials used for automation.</p><h3 id="problem-it-solves-1" tabindex="-1">Problem it solves <a class="header-anchor" href="#problem-it-solves-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Problem it solves&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Removes constant signing friction while preventing unlimited delegated authority.</p><h3 id="why-it-matters-1" tabindex="-1">Why it matters <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-it-matters-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why it matters&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Users can automate in controlled windows and revoke access when strategy or risk context changes.</p><h2 id="selective-disclosure" tabindex="-1">Selective Disclosure <a class="header-anchor" href="#selective-disclosure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Selective Disclosure&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Selective disclosure means proving a constrained claim without publishing full underlying history.</p><h3 id="problem-it-solves-2" tabindex="-1">Problem it solves <a class="header-anchor" href="#problem-it-solves-2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Problem it solves&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Users and integrations often need verifiable claims without full strategy exposure.</p><h3 id="why-it-matters-2" tabindex="-1">Why it matters <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-it-matters-2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why it matters&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Supports privacy-preserving collaboration with verifiers, counterparties, and internal policy processes.</p><h2 id="risk-passport" tabindex="-1">Risk Passport <a class="header-anchor" href="#risk-passport" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Risk Passport&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Risk Passport is a composed trust view that combines reputation, identity, onboarding, and receipt-linked context.</p><h3 id="problem-it-solves-3" tabindex="-1">Problem it solves <a class="header-anchor" href="#problem-it-solves-3" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Problem it solves&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Eliminates fragmented “check 8 endpoints manually” workflows.</p><h3 id="why-it-matters-3" tabindex="-1">Why it matters <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-it-matters-3" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why it matters&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Gives users and integrators a compact operational posture for decision support.</p><h2 id="concept-relationship-map" tabindex="-1">Concept Relationship Map <a class="header-anchor" href="#concept-relationship-map" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Concept Relationship Map&quot;">​</a></h2><div class="language-mermaid vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">mermaid</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">flowchart TB</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  SK[Session Keys] --&gt; EX[Execution behavior]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  PF[Proof-aware flows] --&gt; EX</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  RP[Risk Passport] --&gt; EX</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  SD[Selective disclosure] --&gt; CM[Compliance workflows]</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">  EX --&gt; RC[Receipts and timelines]</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Next: <a href="/docs/flow.html">How execution flows</a> | <a href="/docs/session-keys.html">Session keys</a> | <a href="/docs/risk-passport.html">Risk Passport</a></p>', 34)
